      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Three distinct artifacts:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Agenda - written before the meeting. Forward-looking.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Minutes - written during/after. Outcomes, decisions, action items, dissent on the record. Backward-looking and durable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Decision Log / ADR - written when a decision is significant enough to outlive the meeting. One decision per record, indexed, immutable once accepted.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The four load-bearing fields",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every captured decision must answer:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#1-the-four-load-bearing-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "What was decided - a single declarative sentence, not a description of the debate.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#1-the-four-load-bearing-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Why - the one or two reasons that tipped it. Trade-offs accepted. Alternatives rejected.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#1-the-four-load-bearing-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Who owns it - exactly one named person per action item. Co-ownership is no ownership.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#1-the-four-load-bearing-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "When - a specific date, not \"soon\" or \"next sprint\".",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#1-the-four-load-bearing-fields",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Agenda vs minutes — separate documents, different tense",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Agenda items are intent (\"discuss pricing tier rollout\"). Minutes items are outcome (\"decided to defer pricing tier rollout to Q3; revisit June 15 sync\").",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#2-agenda-vs-minutes-separate-documents-different-tense",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Sync vs async minutes",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Sync minutes (live meeting): Capture only what is needed to reconstruct outcomes. Skip the back-and-forth. Aim for ~10% the length of the conversation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#3-sync-vs-async-minutes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Async minutes (Slack thread, Loom comment chain): The thread is the discussion. The minutes job is to write the synthesis at the top.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#3-sync-vs-async-minutes",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Verbatim quote vs paraphrase",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use a verbatim quote in three cases only:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#4-verbatim-quote-vs-paraphrase",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "On-the-record dissent",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#4-verbatim-quote-vs-paraphrase",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A specific commitment",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#4-verbatim-quote-vs-paraphrase",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A regulatory / legal trigger",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#4-verbatim-quote-vs-paraphrase",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Everywhere else, paraphrase.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#4-verbatim-quote-vs-paraphrase",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Decisions live in a log, not in the meeting file",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Significant decisions should be extracted into a separate decision log (or ADR file) with a stable ID, indexed, and linked back to the meeting.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#5-decisions-live-in-a-log-not-in-the-meeting-file",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. The ADR form for technical decisions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Michael Nygard's 2011 template: Title · Status · Context · Decision · Consequences",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#6-the-adr-form-for-technical-decisions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Status moves through: proposed → accepted → deprecated → superseded by ADR-NNNN. ADRs are never deleted or edited substantively after acceptance - they are superseded by a new ADR that links back.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#6-the-adr-form-for-technical-decisions",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Capture dissent on the record",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Name the dissenter and one-sentence their objection. \"Anonymous 'concerns were raised'\" is useless and reads as cover.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#7-capture-dissent-on-the-record",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Outcome-oriented language",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Bad: \"We talked about the latency issue for a while.\" Good: \"Decided to roll back the v2.3 caching change; Priya owns rollback PR by Wed.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#8-outcome-oriented-language",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Every bullet should start with a verb of outcome (decided, agreed, deferred, rejected, assigned, scheduled, escalated).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#8-outcome-oriented-language",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. Distribute fast, freeze faster",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Minutes that go out 5 days later are minutes nobody reads. Target: same-day or next-morning.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/meeting-minutes-and-decision-log/#9-distribute-fast-freeze-faster",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
